  "final_report": "- Physical interpretation: the derived dominant combination is algebraically Re^{3/4}(r/D), implying cf is driven by inertial strength (Re^{3/4}) and amplified linearly by wall roughness (r/D) while viscosity enters via Re. Validation caveat: no single classical identity (empirical dominant fit).\n- RAG grounding: expression uses retrieved Reynolds number (Re = rho U D / mu) and relative roughness (r/D); this is not equal to a single documented dimensionless number but combines those two. Cf is the skin‑friction coefficient Cf = tau_w/(0.5 rho U^2), linking the combination to wall shear.",
